/* محتوى مادة physiology (الدم فقط لحد ما ينزل باقي المادة): بنك أسئلة د. محمد ماهر. مولَّد من tools/gen_physiology.py */
(function(M){(M.pkg=M.pkg||{})["physiology"]={"headA": "<div class=\"eyebrow\">Physiology · Dr. Mohamed Maher MCQs<\/div>", "headB": "<p class=\"lede\">أسئلة اختيار من متعدد في الدم (علم وظائف الأعضاء) من بنك أسئلة د. محمد ماهر، بمفاتيحها المطبوعة في جدول المفاتيح. هذا أول فصل نزل من المادة، وباقي الفصول بتتضاف لما تنزل.<\/p><div class=\"stats\"><div><b>1<\/b><span>فصل<\/span><\/div><div><b>9<\/b><span>قسمًا<\/span><\/div><div><b>185<\/b><span>سؤال بمفتاح<\/span><\/div><\/div>", "body": "<main><section id=\"tab-galal\" class=\"tabpane\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><div class=\"card-bar\"><p class=\"note\">أسئلة اختيار من متعدد في الدم (علم وظائف الأعضاء) من بنك أسئلة د. محمد ماهر، بمفاتيحها المطبوعة في جدول المفاتيح. هذا أول فصل نزل من المادة، وباقي الفصول بتتضاف لما تنزل.<\/p><\/div><div class=\"gnav\"><label for=\"gSel\">القسم:<\/label><select id=\"gSel\"><option value=\"\">كل الأقسام (185 سؤال)<\/option><optgroup label=\"Chapter 1 — Blood\" data-src=\"maher\" data-srclabel=\"Dr. Mohamed Maher MCQs\"><option value=\"ph1_t01\">Body Fluids (9)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t02\">Measurement of Body Fluids &amp; Homeostasis (8)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t03\">Plasma Proteins (31)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t04\">Erythrocytes &amp; Erythropoiesis (30)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t05\">Vitamin B12 (17)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t06\">Iron (26)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t07\">Anemia &amp; Polycythemia (14)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t08\">Hemostasis (37)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t09\">Blood Groups &amp; Rh (13)<\/option><\/optgroup><\/select><\/div><div class=\"gpart\" data-part=\"1\" data-ch=\"p1\"><h2 dir=\"ltr\">Chapter 1 · Blood <small>— الدم · 185 سؤال · <bdi dir=\"ltr\">Dr. Mohamed Maher MCQs<\/bdi><\/small><\/h2><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t01\"><h3>Body Fluids <small>— 9 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t01\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-001\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">1- Most of the body weight is formed of:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Proteins<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Water<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fats<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Minerals<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-002\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">2- One of the following cations is present in large amounts in the intracellular fluid:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sodium<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Potassium<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Magnesium<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Calcium<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-003\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">3- The following electrolytes are present at higher concentration in the extracellular fluid than in the intracellular fluid, except :<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Na⁺<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- K⁺<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Cl⁻<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- HCO3⁻<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-004\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">4- Extracellular fluid and intracellular fluids are similar in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Concentration of potassium ions<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Osmolality<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Concentration of sodium ions<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Concentration of calcium ions<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-005\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">5- The extracellular fluid:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Comprises 40% of the body weight<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Contains K⁺ as chief cations and protein and phosphates as chief anions<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Contains Na⁺ as chief cations and CI⁻ and HCO₃⁻ as chief anions<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Has slightly acidic pH<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-006\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">6- Which of the following is in a higher concentration in ICF than ECF<span class=\"gtag\" dir=\"ltr\">Past exam<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ca<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- PO4<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Na<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- HCO3<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-007\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">7- The intracellular fluid<span class=\"gtag\" dir=\"ltr\">Past exam<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Accounts for 80 % of total body weight<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Includes 5% intravascular fluid and 15% interstitial fluid<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Has the same osmolarity as plasma<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Main cation is sodium<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-008\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">8- Which of the following is the main cation extracellularly<span class=\"gtag\" dir=\"ltr\">Past exam<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sodium<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Potassium<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Magnesium<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Glucose<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-009\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">9- All are in higher concentration in ICF than ECF except<span class=\"gtag\" dir=\"ltr\">Past exam<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Mg<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- K<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- PO4<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- HCO3<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t02\"><h3>Measurement of Body Fluids &amp; Homeostasis <small>— 8 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t02\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-010\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">10- Heavy water and inulin are injected into a normal 40-year-old man. The volume of distribution of heavy water was 42 L and that of inulin 14 L:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The man's plasma volume is about 7L<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The man's intracellular fluid volume is about 14 L<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The man's total body water cannot be determined from these data<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The man's intracellular fluid volume is about 28 L<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-011\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">11- Which of the following substances or combinations of substances could be used to measure interstitial fluid volume?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Mannitol<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Evans blue<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Inulin and heavy water (D2O(<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Inulin and radioactive albumin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-012\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">12- Which of the following marker administrated intravenously distributes exclusively in intracellular fluid?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Evans blue dye<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heavy water<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Sucrose<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-013\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">13- One gram of inulin was injected into a woman. After equilibration, a plasma sample had an inulin concentration of 0.08 g/L. During the equilibration period, 20% of the injected inulin was excreted in the urine<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The subject’s extracellular fluid (ECF) volume is 1 L<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Intracellular fluid (ICF) volume is 1 L<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- ECF volume is 10 L<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- ICF volume is 10 L<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Interstitial volume is 12.5 L<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-014\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">14- Which statement is incorrect?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- \"Homeostasis\" describes the maintenance of constant conditions in body<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- In most diseases, homeostatic mechanisms are no longer operating<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The body's compensatory mechanisms often lead to deviations from the normal range in some of the body's functions<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Disease is generally considered to be a state of disrupted homeostasis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-015\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">15- Which statement about feedback control systems is incorrect?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Most control systems of the body act by negative feedback<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Positive feedback usually promotes stability in a system<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Uterine contractions during labour involves positive feedback<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Feed-forward control is important in regulating muscle activity<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-016\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">16- Homeostasis includes all of the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Blood pH has a limited range of variation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Osmolality of the extracellular fluid is kept constant at 300 mosmol/L<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Most of the hormones are controlled by negative feedback mechanism<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Body temperature changes markedly with changes in environmental temperature<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-017\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">17- Homeostasis can be considered:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The maintenance of a dynamically stable internal environment<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The maintenance of a static yet stable internal environment<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- An internal environment that changes as the external environment changes<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- A situation where the degree of internal change is proportional to the square of the degree of external change<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t03\"><h3>Plasma Proteins <small>— 31 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t03\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-018\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">18- The most important function of albumin is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Acting as an antibody<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Contributing to the clotting process<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Contributing to the effective osmotic pressure of plasma<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Responsible for viscosity of blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-019\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">19- Which of the following substances is present in plasma but not in serum?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Globulins<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Fibrinogen<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Erythrocytes<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Inorganic ions<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-020\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">20- Concerning the synthesis of plasma proteins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- All types are formed by the liver only<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Albumin, globulins and 50% of fibrinogen are formed by the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Gamma globulins are formed by plasma cells in the lymphoid organs<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Gamma globulins are released from activated T-lymphocytes<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-021\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">21- All the following about the osmotic pressure of plasma are correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The total osmotic pressure of plasma is largely due to the contribution of NaCl ions<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The effective colloidal osmotic pressure of plasma is about 28mmHg<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The colloidal osmotic pressure of plasma favors the filtration of fluid outside capillaries<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-022\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">22- Concerning plasma proteins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- They include clotting factors<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Globulins are formed mainly in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrinogen has the highest concentration<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Albumin has the largest molecular weight<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Albumin is mainly formed by the reticulo-endothelial system<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-023\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">23- All the following about plasma proteins is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are mainly formed in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Deficiency produces edema<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Prevent the loss of iron and vitamin B₁₂ in urine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are positively charged at pH 7.4<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Are sources of tissue proteins<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-024\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">24- Regarding plasma all is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Contains antibodies<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Its normal content of proteins is 7.4 mg%<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It clots on standing<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is yellow in color<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is part of ECF<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- Represents 55% of total blood volume<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-025\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">25- Albumin contributes maximally to oncotic pressure because it has:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Low concentration<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- High concentration<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-026\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">26- All the following about albumin is true, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Contributes more to plasma colloid osmotic pressure than globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Filters freely at the renal glomeruli<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is negatively charged at the normal pH of blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is mainly synthesized by the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Has the smallest MW<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-027\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">27- The plasma protein with the lowest molecular weight is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Albumin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Beta- globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ceruloplasmin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Gamma-globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Transferrin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-028\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">28- Albumin/Globulin ratio:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Normally equals 1.2: 1.6<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is higher in liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is increased in albuminuria<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased in infections<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Can estimate liver and spleen functions<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-029\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">29- Concerning plasma proteins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Globulins are responsible for the osmotic function<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The oncotic pressure is 5000 mmHg<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Albumin has the highest concentration<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Fibrinogen has the smallest molecular weight<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Prothrombin has a transport function<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-030\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">30- One of the following is not a function of plasma protein:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Transport of hormones<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Maintenance of colloidal osmotic pressure<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Buffering of blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Blood clotting<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Phagocytosis of bacteria<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-031\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">31- Concerning plasma all the following statements are correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Osmotic pressure is 5000 mmHg.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Osmotic pressure is the sum of crystalloid and colloidal osmotic pressure.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Globulins are responsible for most of the plasma colloidal osmotic pressure.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Differs from serum in that serum contains no fibrinogen<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-032\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">32- Which of the following cells if selectively destroyed will affect antibody production?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Eosinophils<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Macrophages<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Neutrophils<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Plasma cells<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- T- lymphocytes<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-033\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">33- The amount of plasma proteins (=P.P.) is near to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- 10 gm %.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- 7 gm %.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- 1 gm %.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- 30 gm%.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-034\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">34- The plasma proteins perform all the following functions except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- They exert an osmotic force.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- They have a buffering action.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- They increase the capillary permeability.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- They play a role in the body defense mechanisms.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-035\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">35- The plasma albumin is specially needed for:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Immunity.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Production of osmotic pressure.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Blood coagulation.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- All of the above.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-036\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">36- The A/G ratio is important clinically in detecting:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Liver disease.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Cardiac disease.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Nervous disease.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Lung disease.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-037\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">37- The plasma gamma globulins are synthesized mainly in the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heart<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Lungs.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Lymphoid (reticuloendothelial) system.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-038\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">38- The Viscosity produced by plasma proteins is mainly due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Prothrombin.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Albumin.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrinogen.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- All of the above.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-039\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">39- About the following abnormalities and their reasons, all are true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The A/G ratio is reduced in liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Tissue fluid formation increases in cases of hypoproteinaemia .<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Albumin is increased in infection<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-040\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">40- All the following are functions of the plasma proteins except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Control of the plasma volume.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Control of erythropoiesis= formation of new RBCs<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Transport of hormones.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-041\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">41- All the following about plasma albumin is true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It makes the greatest contribution to the plasma oncotic pressure.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is minimally filtered at the renal glomeruli.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It behaves as an anion at the blood pH.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It is involved in the production of immunity.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-042\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">42- In the plasma:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Water constitutes about 60 % of its total volume.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The main cation is sodium at a concentration of 42 mEq /litre.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The concentration of plasma proteins is about 7 gm %.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The inorganic constituents’ concentration is 0.19 %.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-043\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">43- The colloidal osmotic pressure of the plasma is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Mainly caused by the plasma fibrinogen content.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Responsible for diffusion of water and solutes out of the capillaries.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- About 300 milliosmoles /litre.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- About (28 mmHg).<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-044\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">44- Plasma proteins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are formed in liver only<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Have a level of 7.2 gm/L<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Represent 85% of the buffering power of blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-045\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">45- Albumin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is normally filtered freely by the kidneys due to its relatively small molecular size<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is positively charged at the normal pH of blood and acts as a cation<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is responsible for the transport function due to its elongated shape<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is important for the regulation of fluid exchange across capillary membrane<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-046\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">46- The osmotic function of plasma proteins depends mainly on:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Albumin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrinogen<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Prothrombin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-047\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">47- Gamma globulins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are formed by red blood corpuscles<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Are formed by the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Are formed by the bone marrow<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are formed by plasma cells of lymphoid tissue<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-048\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">48- Human plasma albumin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Contributes less to plasma colloid osmotic pressure than globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Filters freely at the renal glomerulus<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is negatively charged at the normal pH of blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Carries carbon dioxide in blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t04\"><h3>Erythrocytes &amp; Erythropoiesis <small>— 30 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t04\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-049\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">49- Erythrocytes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are rigid biconcave cells<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Have an average diameter of 80µ<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Have a life span of 180 days<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are responsible for the major part of blood viscosity<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Have a mean cell volume of 60 µ³<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-050\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">50- Concerning the RBC:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Its life span is 120 days<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is produced by the liver and spleen in fetus<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- All the above are correct<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-051\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">51- The membrane of RBCs allows the following except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increase the inner tension with the increase in volume<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pass within small capillaries without rupture<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increase the surface area for gas exchange<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Keep hemoglobin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-052\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">52- The size of RBCs increases in venous blood because of:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Venous blood is more alkaline than arterial blood<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Carrying CO2<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increased content of Na⁺ inside RBCs<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased content of K⁺ inside RBCs<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-053\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">53- The iron of the hemoglobin is eventually:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Converted into transferrin in the large intestine<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Converted into ferritin in the kidney<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Excreted from the body<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- All of the above<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- None of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-054\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">54- All the following about hemoglobin is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It carries oxygen from the lungs to transport it to the tissues<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It contains 4 atoms of iron in the ferrous state<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It consists of 4 polypeptide chains and 4 heme groups<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- After it combines with oxygen molecules the iron changes to ferric state<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The globin part forms carbamino compounds with CO₂<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-055\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">55- hematocrit value of 45 % means that:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- 45% of the Hb is in the plasma.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- 45 % of the total blood volume is made up of plasma.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- 45 % of the total blood volume is made up of blood cells.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- 45 % of the Hb is in the red blood cells.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-056\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">56- The polypeptides in the globin part of normal adult Hb consists of:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- 2 alpha and 2 beta chains.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- 2 alpha and 2 gamma chains.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- 2 alpha and 2 delta chains.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- 2 beta and 2 gamma chains.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-057\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">57- Blood cell destruction occurs mainly in the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Bone marrow.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Kidneys<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Heart.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Spleen.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-058\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">58- About erythrocytes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- They contain no enzymes.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- They are responsible for the major part of blood viscosity.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Their life span is about 2 months.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Their Hb content carries only O2.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-059\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">59- Erythropoiesis in adult individuals occurs normally in the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Red bone marrow.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Yellow bone marrow.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Spleen.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-060\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">60- In the following, mark the wrong statement:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Some substances (e.g. thyroid hormones) circulate bound to plasma proteins to increase their buffering capacity.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hb is present inside the R.B.Cs to prevent its escape to the plasma and excretion in the urine.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Erythropoiesis is increased in normal animals when injected with plasma obtained from hypoxic animals.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-061\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">61- About the active erythropoietic tissue, all the following is true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is not found in the vertebrae of adults.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is present early in intrauterine life.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It occupies the whole bone marrow at birth.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It is replaced by fat in the shafts of long bones in healthy adults.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-062\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">62- Erythropoiesis:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Occurs in the liver during the first 5 years of life<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Above 20 occurs in the bone marrow of all bones<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is affected by vitamin K deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is stimulated at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is more stimulated in females than males<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-063\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">63- Concerning erythropoiesis all is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is decreased after bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Needs healthy liver for formation of globin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Needs healthy kidney for formation of 15% of erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is stimulated by testosterone hormone<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Increases in response to hypoxia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-064\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">64- Concerning erythropoiesis all is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is decreased after bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Needs healthy liver for formation of globin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Needs healthy kidney for formation of 15% of erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is stimulated by testosterone hormone<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-065\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">65- Erythropoietin is essential for:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Leukopoiesis.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Formation of prothrombin.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Formation of red blood corpuscles.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-066\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">66- Erythropoietin hormone:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is secreted mainly by the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is secreted mainly by the pancreas<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Stimulates RBCs formation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Stimulates WBCs formation<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-067\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">67- The main site of production of erythropoietin is the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bone marrow.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Spleen.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Kidneys.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-068\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">68- Erythropoietin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is secreted by red bone marrow<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is stimulated by estrogen hormone<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is a component of hemoglobin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is secreted 85% from the liver and 15% from the bone marrow<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is elevated in persons living at high altitude<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-069\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">69- Erythropoietin hormone:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is secreted by the kidney 85% and the bone marrow 15%<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is stimulated by cobalt salts and acidosis at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Stimulates mitosis of the sensitive uncommitted stem cells<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Speeds all steps of development of proerythroblasts to mature RBCs<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-070\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">70- Erythropoietin hormone is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Secreted by the kidney 15% and the liver 85%<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Stimulated by acidosis at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Synthesized and released by red blood cell<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Inhibited by adenosine antagonists<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-071\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">71- A 36-year-old man with end stage renal disease has normocytic normochromic anemia. Which of the following is the most appropriate therapy?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Ferrous sulphate<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin B6<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Vitamin B₁₂<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-072\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">72- Erythrocytes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Synthesize and release erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Have a higher concentration of potassium than is in plasma<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Have an abundant supply of mitochondria<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Have a multilobed nucleus<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Have about a 7 day survival time after release into the blood<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- Contain major histocompatibility protein (MHC) class I<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-073\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">73- The synthesis and release of erythropoietin is increased in a person who goes to live at high altitude because:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Cardiac output is increased<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hematocrit is increased<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Partial pressure of oxygen is less<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Alveolar ventilation rate is increased<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-074\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">74- Concerning erythropoiesis all the following statements are correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It occurs in the liver and spleen during fetal life.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- All blood cells are derived from a common uncommitted stem cell.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Erythropoietin hormone is secreted mainly by the liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It is inhibited after exposure to atomic radiation.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-075\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">75- Concerning the RBC:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It has a diameter of about 5 µm<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Contain hemoglobin, ribosomes and mitochondria<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is produced by the liver and spleen in fetus<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increase the inner tension with the increase in volume<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-076\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">76- Concerning erythropoiesis:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Needs healthy liver for formation of Heme<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Needs healthy kidney for formation of 15% of erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is stimulated by testosterone and thyroxine hormones<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Occurs in the liver during the first 5 years of life<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-077\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">77- The synthesis and release of erythropoietin is increased in a person who goes to live at high altitude because:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Partial pressure of oxygen is less<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Cardiac output is increased<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Acidosis at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Alveolar ventilation rate is increased<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-078\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">78- A 36-year-old man with end stage renal disease has normocytic normochromic anemia. Which of the following is the most appropriate therapy?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferrous sulphate<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin B12<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t05\"><h3>Vitamin B12 <small>— 17 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t05\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-079\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">79- Concerning Vitamin B12 absorption:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It needs intrinsic factor secreted by parietal cells of duodenum<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is absorbed by simple diffusion at lower ileum<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is transported in blood bound to transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Deficiency of pancreatic trypsin decreases its rate of absorption<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-080\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">80- Concerning Vitamin B12 absorption:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It needs intrinsic factor secreted by parietal cells of duodenum<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Absorbed by pinocytosis at lower ileum<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is transported in blood bound to transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Deficiency of pancreatic trypsin increases its rate of absorption<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-081\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">81- Improper maturation of the red blood corpuscles can be caused by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Vitamin B12 deficiency.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hypoxia.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Iron deficiency.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Bone marrow aplasia.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-082\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">82- The intrinsic factor:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is found in the liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is produced by the gastric parietal cells.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is secreted by the terminal ileum.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Aids absorption of folic acid.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-083\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">83- Vitamin B₁₂ or folic acid deficiency produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Erythroblastic cells of the bone marrow to become smaller than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The adult red blood cells to become smaller than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The adult red blood cells to have a thicker membrane than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The adult red blood cells to become larger than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The adult red blood cells to exhibit increased osmotic fragility<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-084\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">84- Vitamin B₁₂:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Deficiency produces normocytic anemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Needs gastric HCl for its absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is absorbed from the upper part of the small intestine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is needed for nuclear maturation and cell division.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is stored in the bone marrow<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-085\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">85- Synthesis of DNA and cell division requires:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Iron<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Vitamin B₁₂ and folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Proteins of plant origin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin C<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-086\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">86- Macrocytic anemia is due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Chronic blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Iron deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin B12 or folic acid deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Acute blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- RBCs hemolysis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-087\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">87- Vitamin B12 deficiency may<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Result from disease of the proximal part of the ileum.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Result in anemia with small RBCs well filled with haemoglobin.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Cause a reduction in the circulating platelet level.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cause pathological changes in the central nervous system.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-088\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">88- Failure to absorb vitamin B₁₂ from the gastrointestinal tract results in a disease called:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hypochromic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pernicious anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Polycythemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Thalassaemia<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Normochromic anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-089\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">89- All the following substances are essential for the normal development of R.B.Cs except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Folic acid.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Ascorbic acid.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Nicotinic acid.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cyanocobalamine.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-090\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">90- Why is vitamin B12 necessary for erythropoiesis?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It's necessary for the ejection of the RBC nucleus<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It's necessary for DNA synthesis<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It's essential for protein aggregation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It's essential for oxygen's nucleophilic reaction with hemoglobin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-091\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">91- Stomach plays important role in erythropoiesis because it:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Helps absorption of folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Helps absorption of B12 and iron<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Secretes erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Forms globin part of hemoglobin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-092\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">92- In pernicious anaemia:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The life span of R.B.C.s is longer than normal.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- There is microcytic hyperchromic anaemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The formation of macrocytes is decreased.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Decreased absorption of vitamin B12 is suspected.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-093\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">93- Pernicious anaemia may be all the following except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sometimes the result of the malabsorption syndrome.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Treated with iron.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The cause of peripheral neuropathy.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Associated with carcinoma of the stomach.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-094\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">94- Vitamin B12 deficiency may:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Result from disease of the duodenum<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Result in anemia with large fragile RBCs<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Decrease the formation of platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cause leucopenia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-095\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">95- Vitamin B12 or folic acid deficiency produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Erythroblastic cells of the bone marrow to become smaller than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The adult red blood cells to become smaller than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The adult red blood cells to have a thicker membrane than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The adult red blood cells to become larger than normal<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t06\"><h3>Iron <small>— 26 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t06\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-096\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">96- As regard the iron required for hemoglobin synthesis:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferric iron (Fe³⁺) is absorbed from the upper part of the small intestine<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is transported in the blood in the form of transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Its deficiency produces macrocytic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The greatest percentage of ferritin is found in the bone marrow<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-097\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">97- Iron:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is absorbed as ferrous (Fe²⁺) iron by a passive process<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is decreased in acute blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is stored in the liver in the form of transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Needs vitamin C for absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Deficiency produces pernicious anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-098\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">98- Iron absorption:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Occurs when the iron is in the ferric state (Fe³⁺)<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Requires gastric HCl<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is a passive process which depends on the body requirements<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Occurs in the lower part of the small intestine<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-099\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">99- Microcytic hypochromic anemia is due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Decrease vitamin B₁₂ intake<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decrease iron intake<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Diseases of the heart<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Diseases of the lung<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Acute massive bleeding<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-100\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">100- All about iron absorption is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Antacids reduce iron absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heme iron is better absorbed than non-heme iron<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ferrous iron (Fe²⁺) is better absorbed than ferric iron (Fe³⁺)<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The majority of iron absorption occurs in terminal ileum<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-101\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">101- Which of the following statements about iron metabolism is correct?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferritin is a plasma protein that transports iron in the blood<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hemosiderin is a product of hemoglobin degradation<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Iron is more efficiently absorbed in the ferrous state than in the ferric state<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Most iron in the body is stored as hemosiderin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The gastrointestinal rate of iron absorption is extremely high<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-102\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">102- Iron deficiency:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is more common in males than in females<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- May cause anemia by inhibiting the rate of multiplication of RBCs stem cells<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Occurs due to chronic blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- May cause large pale erythrocytes to appear in peripheral blood<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Anemia must be treated by iron injection<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-103\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">103- In the blood, iron is primarily transported by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hemosiderin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Ferritin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Stercobilin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Transferrin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-104\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">104- The major protein that transports iron in the plasma from the site of absorption to cells engaged in erythropoiesis is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hepcidin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ferritin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Hemosiderin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-105\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">105- Most of the iron in the body is present in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hemoglobin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Myoglobin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ferritin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Transferrin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-106\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">106- About iron deficiency anaemia:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is more common in men than in women.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is characterized by large pale erythrocytes.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is typically found following chronic blood loss from the body.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It occurs in gastric diseases associated with lack of the intrinsic factor.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-107\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">107- The production of erythrocytes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is decreased in high altitudes.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Occurs in the spleen in normal adults.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is stimulated by an increase in the arterial PCO2.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is decreased if the stomach loses the ability to produce a normal gastric juice.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-108\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">108- The red cells in iron deficiency anemia are:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Normocytic normochromic.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Spherocytic cells.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Microcytic hypochromic<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Macrocytic hyperchromic.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-109\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">109- An 18-year-old girl was prescribed iron supplement by her doctor as she was thought to take a diet deficient in iron. Lack of iron often causes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Polycythemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hypochromic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Pernicious anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Megaloblastic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Normochromic anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-110\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">110- Hepcidin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Stimulates formation of ferroportin molecules in macrophages<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Secretion is inhibited by inflammation and hypoxia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Inhibits the release of recycled iron from macrophage<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is a hormone secreted by the enterocyte to regulate iron intestinal absorption<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-111\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">111- Which of the following protein is a regulator for iron absorption by enterocytes<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferritin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hemosiderin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Hepcidin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Transferrin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-112\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">112- Which of the following statements about iron metabolism is correct?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferritin is a plasma protein that transports iron in the blood<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Iron is more efficiently absorbed in the ferrous state than in the ferric state<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Most iron in the body is stored as hemosiderin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The gastrointestinal rate of iron absorption is extremely high<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-113\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">113- Iron deficiency:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is more common in males than in females<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- May cause anemia by inhibiting the division of RBCs stem cells<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- May cause small pale erythrocytes to appear in peripheral blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Occurs due to acute blood loss<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-114\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">114- Iron deficiency:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is more common in males than in females<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- May cause anemia by inhibiting the division of RBCs stem cells<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Occurs due to chronic blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- May cause large pale erythrocytes to appear in peripheral blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-115\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">115- Stomach plays important role in erythropoiesis because It:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Helps absorption of folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Helps absorption of B12 and iron<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Secretes erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Forms globin part of hemoglobin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-116\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">116- Iron absorption is characterized by all of the following EXCEPT:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It needs vitamin C to facilitate its absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heme iron is directly absorbed through heme carrier protein<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It occurs at the distal part of the small intestine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Absorbed iron is carried by transferrin in plasma<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-117\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">117- Iron:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is decreased in acute blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is stored in the liver in the form of transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Needs vitamin C for absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Deficiency produces pernicious anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-118\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">118- Iron absorption:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Occurs when the iron is in the ferric state (Fe3*)<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Requires gastric HCl<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is a passive process which depends on the body requirements<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Occurs in the lower part of the small intestine<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-119\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">119- Iron deficiency<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Frequently follows persistent loss of blood from the body.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is more common in men than in women.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Cause anemia by inhibiting the rate of multiplication of RBC stem cells.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- May cause large pale erythrocytes to appear in peripheral blood.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-120\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">120- About iron deficiency anaemia:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is more common in adult men<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is characterized by large pale erythrocytes.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is typically found following chronic blood loss from the body.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It occurs in gastric diseases associated with lack of intrinsic factor.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-121\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">121- An 18-year-old girl was prescribed iron supplement by her doctor as she was thought to take a diet deficient in iron. Lack of iron often causes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Polycythemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hypochromic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Pernicious anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Normochromic anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t07\"><h3>Anemia &amp; Polycythemia <small>— 14 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t07\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-122\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">122- All the following conditions cause anemia except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Erythroblastosis fetalis.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Vitamin B12 deficiency.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Hypothyroidism.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Living at high altitudes.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-123\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">123- Severe depression of the bone marrow may result in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Microcytic hypochromic anaemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Increased number of granulocytes.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Aplastic anaemia, leucopenia, and thrombocytopenia.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased coagulability of the blood.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-124\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">124- The red blood corpuscles:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Haemolyze when placed in a hypertonic solution.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Are smaller than normal in case of folic acid deficiency.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Are normal in size in anemia due to bone marrow depression.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-125\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">125- Anemia results from all the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Living at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Atrophy of gastric mucosa<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Iron deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Folic acid deficiency<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-126\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">126- Excessive destruction of erythrocytes is characteristic of:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Aplastic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pernicious anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Hemolytic anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-127\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">127- Concerning polycythemia the following is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Occurs in liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Increases the viscosity of the blood<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Can occur in someone who lives at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Can result from a high level of erythropoietin secretion<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-128\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">128- Increased R. B.Cs fragility occurs in all the following cases except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sickle cell anaemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Iron deficiency anaemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Hereditary spherocytosis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-129\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">129- Polycythemia may occur in all the following conditions except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Tumor of the kidney.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Right to left shunts in the heart.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Advanced liver disease.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- High altitudes.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-130\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">130- Severe depression of the bone marrow may result in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Microcytic hypochromic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Increased number of granulocytes<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Aplastic anemia, leucopenia, and thrombocytopenia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased coagulability of the blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-131\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">131- Causes of Microcytic Hypochromic anemia, all are true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Iron deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Acute bleeding<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Partial gastrectomy<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Excessive menses<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-132\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">132- Conditions cause normocytic normochromic anemia, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Acute hemorrhage<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hemolytic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Aplastic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Folic acid deficiency anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-133\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">133- Microcytic hypochromic anemia is due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Decrease vitamin B12 intake<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decrease iron intake<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Diseases of the heart<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Diseases of the lung<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-134\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">134- Macrocytic anemia is due to<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Chronic blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Iron deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin B12 or folic acid deficiency<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-135\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">135- Normocytic Normochromic anemia is characterized by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Normal RBCs count, normal RBCs size and normal hemoglobin content<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Normal RBCs count, normal RBCs size and low hemoglobin content<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Normal RBCs count, normal RBCs size and normal PCV<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Normal RBCs size, low RBCs count and low hemoglobin content<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t08\"><h3>Hemostasis <small>— 37 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t08\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-136\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">136- The first phase of hemostasis is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Separation of globin and heme<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Activation of Prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Platelet aggregation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vascular spasm<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-137\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">137- Thromboxane A₂:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Causes platelet aggregation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is metabolized to prostacyclin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is directly inactivated by binding to aspirin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Converts prothrombin to thrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is released by erythrocytes<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-138\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">138- The phase of coagulation that begins with exposed endothelial collagen is the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Extrinsic pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Intrinsic pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Common pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Fibrin stabilization phase<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-139\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">139- Contact of the blood with sub- endothelial collagen produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Inhibition of platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Activation of factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Activation of factor XII<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Activation of factor IX<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-140\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">140- Blood coagulation:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Through the extrinsic pathway is initiated by contact of blood with a negatively charged surface<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Through the intrinsic pathway does not occur outside the body<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Through the intrinsic pathway is initiated by tissue damage<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Through the extrinsic pathway is initiated by the release of tissue thromboplastin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Results from conversion of thrombin to prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- Can occur in the absence of calcium<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-141\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">141- The correct sequence of activation of extrinsic pathway of blood coagulation is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Tissue thromboplastin activates factor VIII<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Calcium ions activate factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Tissue thromboplastin activates factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Tissue thromboplastin activates factor IX<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Collagen fibers activate factor XII<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-142\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">142- Which sequence is correct for the following events? 1. Fibrinogen --&gt; Fibrin 2. Clot retraction 3. Formation of thromboplastin 4. Prothrombin --&gt; Thrombin<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- 1,2,3,4<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- 3,4,1,2<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- 4,3,1,2<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- 3,2,1,4<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-143\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">143- The following are vitamin K dependent clotting factors, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Factor XII<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Factor X<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-144\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">144- Vitamin K dependent clotting factors include:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Factor IX<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Factor XI<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrinogen<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Plasminogen<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-145\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">145- The final reaction in the formation of a blood clot:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The formation of prothrombin activator<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Thrombin converts fibrinogen to fibrin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Prothrombin activator converts prothrombin to thrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Hageman factor activates prothrombin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-146\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">146- When a blood vessel wall is injured, platelets induce the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Vascular spasm and temporary plug formation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Exposure of platelet phospholipid (PL)<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Initiation of extrinsic pathway of coagulation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Stabilization of fibrin and clot retraction<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-147\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">147- Tissue thromboplastin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is also known as factor V<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is the cell surface receptor for factor VIa<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Complexes with factor VIIa to catalyze the activation of factor X<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is an important component of the intrinsic coagulation pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is normally expressed by endothelial cells<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-148\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">148- Factor VII:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is a cofactor in the coagulation cascade<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Initiates the process of coagulation with tissue thromboplastin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is vitamin-K- independent<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is produced by platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Deficiency is common<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-149\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">149- Which of the following statements regarding coagulation is correct?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Extrinsic pathway activation follows contact of blood with collagen<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It results from conversion of thrombin to prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Prekallikrein is converted to kallikrein during activation of extrinsic pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Thrombin converts fibrinogen to fibrin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Vitamin K is an essential co-factor for hepatic synthesis of factor VIII<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-150\" data-k=\"f\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">150- Normal blood clotting requires:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Inactivation of heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Inactivation of plasmin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Adequate intake of vitamin C<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Adequate intake of vitamin K<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Calcium ions<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- Both (d) and (e) are correct<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-151\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">151- The conversion of fibrinogen to fibrin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is affected by prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is stimulated by heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is reversed by plasmin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is followed by polymerization of fibrin monomers<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-152\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">152- Which of the following is not involved in coagulation?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Gamma globulins<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Calcium<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Vitamin K<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Prothrombin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-153\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">153- Anti thrombin III activity is increased by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Aspirin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Citrate<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Coumarin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Warfarin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-154\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">154- Protein C:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is a major physiological anticoagulant<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decreases the formation of plasmin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is activated by prothrombin to activated protein C<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- In its activated form degrades factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is a breakdown product of C-reactive protein<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-155\" data-k=\"d\" data-alt=\"\" data-fx=\"الـthrombomodulin بيرتبط بالـthrombin ويكوّن مركّبًا بينشّط الـprotein C (مش protein S)، والـprotein S عامل مساعد للـprotein C المنشَّط. فنص الاختيار D غالبًا خطأ مطبعي (المقصود protein C).\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">155- Thrombomodulin:<span class=\"gtag warn\" dir=\"rtl\">مفتاح الملزمة مشكوك فيه<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is secreted by RBCs<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is activated by heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Activates platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Binds with thrombin forming a complex that activates protein S<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-156\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">156- Which of the following is a feature of protein S:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is synthesized by the endothelium<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Its synthesis requires vitamin C<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It functions as a cofactor to protein C<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It is involved in the inactivation of factor IXa<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is involved in the inactivation of factor Xa<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-157\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">157- About the action of anticoagulants, all of the following is true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Dicumarol interferes with the synthesis of prothrombin in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Oxalates form insoluble salts with Ca²⁺<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Citrates and other chelating agents bind Ca²⁺<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Heparin blocks the action of antithrombin III<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-158\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">158- Concerning plasmin one of the following is not correct:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is a proteolytic enzyme<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is formed from plasminogen<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Digests fibrin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Digests fibrinogen<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Has a direct Antithrombin activity<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-159\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">159- Which of the following activates platelets during hemostasis?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Eosinophil degranulation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Exposed collagen or endothelial basement membrane<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrin thread formation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Thromboplastin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-160\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">160- Which one of the following anticoagulants is preferred for storage of donated blood?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Citrate<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Coumarin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Oxalate<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-161\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">161- Bleeding time is prolonged in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Deficiency of factor VIII<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Malabsorption of vitamin K<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Intake of coumarin derivatives<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Intake of large quantities of aspirin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-162\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">162- Prolonged bleeding time may be due to all of the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Thrombocytopenia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hemophilia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Excessive oral intake of aspirin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Both b and c<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-163\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">163- Regarding bleeding from a small cut in the skin all is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is diminished by local vascular spasm<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Stops within about 5 minutes in normal people<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is prolonged in severe factor VIII deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is greater from warm skin than from cold skin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is reduced if the affected limb is elevated<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-164\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">164- Deficiency of factor VIII:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increases the bleeding time<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is due to an abnormal gene on the Y chromosome<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Affects the extrinsic, rather than the intrinsic, pathway for blood coagulation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increases the clotting time<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Causes small (petechial) hemorrhages into the skin to cause purpura<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-165\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">165- Obstruction of common bile duct by a stone will increase bleeding tendency due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Decreased formation of factor XII in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decreased platelet count<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Decreased synthesis of vitamin k in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Decreased synthesis of prothrombin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-166\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">166- How does aspirin influence platelet’s function:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Impairs process of their aggregation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decreases their content<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Reduces bleeding time<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Reduces their life span<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Has no influence<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-167\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">167- Which of the following statements about blood coagulation is correct?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Absence of Ca²⁺ promotes blood coagulation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Patients with hemophilia A usually have a normal bleeding time<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Von Willebrand factor suppresses platelet adhesion<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Von Willebrand factor suppresses blood coagulation<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-168\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">168- Which of the following conditions is associated with a depression of the coagulation process and excessive bleeding after surgery?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Gastrointestinal disease<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heart disease<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Kidney disease<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Pulmonary disease<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-169\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">169- Factor XI:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is produced by platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is a member of the extrinsic pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Activates factor X<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Deficiency causes hemophilia C<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is formed by the spleen<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-170\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">170- Factor IX:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is a co-factor in the coagulation cascade<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is activated by factor V<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Requires prostacyclin for its activity<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Acts by converting factor X to Xa<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Deficiency causes hemophilia A<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-171\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">171- A patient with prolonged activated partial thromboplastin time (APTT). The most likely cause is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Heparin therapy<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Malabsorption of vitamin K<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Poor factor VII synthesis<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Warfarin therapy<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-172\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">172- About intravascular clotting, all the following is true, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It occurs by intrinsic system of coagulation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is induced by slowing of blood flow<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is related to clumping of platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It does not occur normally because Ca²⁺ is present<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- It occurs with accumulation of lipids in the arterial wall<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t09\"><h3>Blood Groups &amp; Rh <small>— 13 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t09\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-173\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">173- Which of the following people would have the most anti-B antibodies?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- An adult male with B+ blood<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- An adult male with O- blood<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- An adult female with B− blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- A female child with AB+ blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-174\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">174- A person has type O+ blood, then which of the following is true?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- He has no agglutinins at all<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- He has no A agglutinogens<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- He has no Rh agglutinogens<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-175\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">175- A person’s blood type was determined to be AB+. Which of the following is true?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- There are no antibodies to antigens A, B, or Rh in the plasma<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The RBCs contain the A and B antigens on their nuclei<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The blood totally lacks the Rh factor<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- He cannot receive blood from someone who is type O negative<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-176\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">176- Which of the following females does not have to be concerned with erythroblastosis fetalis?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- A female with blood type O-<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- A female with blood type O+<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- A female with blood type AB-<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- A female with blood type B+<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- B and d<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-177\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">177- An individual with type B+ blood has which of the following antibodies in their blood?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Anti-A and anti-O<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Anti-B and anti-Rh<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Anti-A<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Anti-B<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Anti-Rh<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-178\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">178- An individual who is blood type AB negative:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Can receive any blood type in moderate amounts except that with the Rh antigen<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Can donate to all blood types in moderate amounts<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Can receive types A, B, and AB but not type O<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Can donate to types A, B, and AB but not to type O<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-179\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">179- Blood type O persons are considered universal donors due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Type O blood has the commonest distribution<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Their RBCs contain neither A nor B agglutinogens<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Their RBCs may contain the Rh-factor<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Their plasma contains both alpha and beta agglutinins<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- They receive blood from all groups<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-180\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">180- A group B Rh-ve person can receive blood for the 2nd time from:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Group AB Rh –ve<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Group O Rh –ve<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Group O Rh +ve<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Group B Rh +ve<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Group A Rh -ve<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-181\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">181- Before blood transfusion, which of the following should be done?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- ESR<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Osmotic fragility test<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Blood indices<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cross matching test<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-182\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">182- Immunoglobulin G:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is produced in large amounts during the primary immune response<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Includes ABO group antibodies<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Activates interferons<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Can cross the placenta to reach the fetus<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Has the largest molecular weight<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-183\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">183- Which one of the following represents the most dangerous situation?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- An Rh-positive mother who is bearing her second Rh-negative child<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- An Rh-negative mother who is bearing her second Rh-positive child<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- An Rh-positive mother who is bearing her first Rh-negative child<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- An Rh-negative mother who is bearing her first Rh-positive child<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The transfusion of O-negative blood into an A-positive recipient<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-184\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">184- All the following statements regarding the ABO and rhesus (Rh) systems are true, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- A person of group O is a universal donor<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- A person who is group AB has anti-A and anti-B antibodies<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The presence of the D antigen means that the subject is Rh+ve<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The second Rh+ve baby of a Rh-ve mother is at a greater risk than the first<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-185\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">185- Erythroblastosis fetalis:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Affects mainly babies of Rh-positive mothers<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Occurs mainly in babies who lack D agglutinogens<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Occurs mainly during the 1st pregnancy<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Can be prevented by injecting the mother with anti-D antibodies just after delivery<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><\/div><\/section><\/main>"}})(window.MG=window.MG||{});
